  "reason": "With zero completed experiments, the priority is to establish a strong, interpretable baseline that future experiments can be compared against. config_029 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) is the most 'standard' multimodal configuration in the space: it uses a well-understood linear RNA encoder (PCA), a strong pretrained image encoder (ImageNet ViT-L), and the simplest aggregation (avgpool) and fusion (concat) options. This makes it a natural reference point. Testing it first lets us (1) gauge whether the multimodal pipeline is viable at all, (2) provide a concrete accuracy/F1 anchor so that subsequent experiments that swap one component (e.g., scgpt vs. PCA, transformer vs. avgpool, weighted vs. concat) can be interpreted as isolated changes from a known baseline, and (3) avoid the risk of over-interpreting a complex configuration before we know what a simple one achieves. It is the highest-information-per-experiment choice under a limited budget because every later design decision can be framed as a controlled deviation from this point."
}

